.TH NVIM-TMUX-OPEN 1 "2026-06-30" "termnav" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nvim-tmux-open \- route terminal open requests into Neovim
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nvim-tmux-open
.B cli
.RI [ nvim-args ...]
.br
.B nvim-tmux-open
.B link
.I target
.RI [ context ...]
.br
.B nvim-tmux-open
.B tmux-link
.I target
.RI [ context ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nvim-tmux-open
opens local or remote terminal targets in an existing Neovim session. The mode
is explicit so normal
.B nvim
command-line arguments stay separate from terminal link text, tmux click text,
and remote-routing metadata.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B cli
Preserve ordinary
.B nvim
argument semantics for a local launcher.
.TP
.B link
Interpret terminal or WezTerm link text and route it to the local or remote
Neovim context when possible.
.TP
.B tmux-link
Interpret a tmux-originated link or click target.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The target was routed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
The requested open operation failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux-follow-click (1),
.BR nvim-link-host (1),
.BR nvim-ssh-control-open (1)
